  "mechanism_d_verdict": "The branch average ((+i0)+(−i0))/2 IS real (the cut discontinuity is exactly 2i·Im, so the average projects to Re). But averaging the two branches is NOT the canonical +i0 dilogarithm prescription — the standard dilogarithm continuation (and the Bloch-Wigner D) commits to ONE branch (+i0). Averaging is a CHOICE (it equals Re by construction), so unless the τ-functor independently selects the symmetric (principal-value) branch, it is CHOSEN-real, not DERIVED-real. The Bloch-Wigner D is the DERIVED real object — it is NOT the average, it is Im Li_2 + log|z|·arg(1−z), a DIFFERENT real number from Re or from the average.",
